Description: portable export and import for libvirt virtual machines
 virtpacker bundles a libvirt domain into a single self-contained
 directory holding the domain XML (with all host paths templated out),
 the disk images, the UEFI nvram variable store, and the swtpm TPM state.
 The directory can be copied to another host and imported, in the same
 spirit as a VMware VM folder.
 .
 On import the bundle is unpacked into the host's standard libvirt
 directories, paths are rewritten, swtpm state is placed at the location
 the domain expects, SELinux labels are restored, and the domain is
 defined. UEFI firmware uses libvirt autoselection so each host supplies
 its own OVMF or edk2 build, which keeps bundles portable across distros.
 .
 The tool drives virsh and qemu-img and is implemented with the Python
 standard library only.
